[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="PassiveDynamicZone" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://g8ycgtxd1y6n" path="res://engine/character/gear_passive/passive_dynamic_zone.gd" id="1_zone"]
[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://b2xlpsu4kynfl" path="res://engine/gamemaster/map/command_zone/dynamic_zone.gd" id="2_shape"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" uid="uid://cqvonn46ieu62" path="res://content/fx_endless/gear/aura/fxe_nanites.tscn" id="3_nanites"]

; THE SHAPE OF THE CLOUD, AND NOTHING ELSE IT NORMALLY CARRIES. A DynamicZone is a real gameplay
; object - it can block sight, fence movement, fence effects and steer the AI - and every one of
; those is a separate export defaulted OFF. Left at their defaults this resource is INERT, and that
; is deliberate: this task is a picture, not a rules change.
;
;   can_see_into / can_see_outof (dynamic_zone.gd:8-9)   both true, so map_state.gd:439-440 never
;       adds the zone to dynamic_zones_that_affect_sight - the only list
;       MapState.does_dynamic_zone_block_sight reads (map_state.gd:211).
;   can_cross_boundary (dynamic_zone.gd:11)              true, so the three places that fence a move
;       on it skip the zone: pathfinder.gd:172 and :361, event_unit_move.gd:388, each guarded by
;       `if not zone.base.can_cross_boundary`.
;   can_effects_cross_boundary (dynamic_zone.gd:12)      true, so map_state.gd:441-442 never pushes
;       the zone into shape.effect_barrier_shards, and the guard that gates
;       UnitTargeting.strip_tiles_from_inaccessible_dynamic_zones - `any(... not
;       can_effects_cross_boundary)` at unit_targeting.gd:207 - stays false, so no targeting set is
;       ever intersected or subtracted against this zone (:210-215).
;   ai_guides (dynamic_zone.gd:15-17)                    0, so is_guide_checked (dynamic_zone.gd:24)
;       is false for every guide and UnitTile.get_tiles_with_guide skips it at unit_tile.gd:755.
;       mt_hive_drone.tres sets AVOID_TRY here because standing in ITS nanites hurts; standing in
;       this cloud is already handled by passive_fungal_network_hostiles.tres, and a second opinion
;       shouted at the AI from a decorative resource would be a balance change nobody asked for.
;
; The one thing left over is bookkeeping: map_state.gd:399-400 records which characters are inside
; every registered zone, and that array is read by exactly one line - map_state.gd:212, inside the
; loop over dynamic_zones_that_affect_sight, which this zone is not in. So it is written and never
; read. THAT IS THE WHOLE RESIDUE of registering a zone for its picture.
[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Resource_shape"]
script = ExtResource("2_shape")
; BURST 2, THE SAME NUMBER passive_fungal_network_hostiles.tres carries as aura_range - and the
; number the author asked to be able to SEE ("a zone effect on the ground, so the burst-2 edge is
; visible"). It is not the ally half's 1: the ally half is a one-tile ring inside this and drawing
; both would be two clouds, not one.
;
; THE TWO FOOTPRINTS ARE COMPUTED BY DIFFERENT CODE AND AGREE ON THE FLAT. The aura asks
; UnitRelation.distance_between, whose horizontal reading is the minimum Tile.distance over CLOSEST
; occupied tiles - max(dx, dy), i.e. Chebyshev (unit_relation.gd:16 into :30-31, and tile.gd:380-387)
; - and is then maxi'd against the elevation distance (unit_relation.gd:19-25). The FX asks
; UnitTile.get_tiles_within(unit, radius, false) (passive_dynamic_zone.gd:24), whose candidate box
; runs from anchor-radius to anchor+radius+unit_size (unit_tile.gd:581-582) - which for this size-2
; frame is exactly Chebyshev 2 from the 2x2 block - and then filters on
; can_unit_touch_tile_elevationwise (:592). So on level ground the drawn set is the caught set; on
; broken ground both fall away with height by arithmetic that is CLOSE but not identical. The
; picture is an honest guide, not a contract, and no spec here claims otherwise.
radius = 2

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_zone")
; A GROUND FX FOR FUNGAL NETWORK. The author playtested QUIETUS MACHINES and said "I dont see a FX
; for the cloud", and chose a zone effect on the ground so the burst-2 edge is visible in play
; (SP2.5 Task 5). This passive draws that and does nothing else: it applies no buff, no status and
; no rule. Everything the card promises is still the two PassiveAuras that carry it
; (passive_fungal_network_allies.tres and _hostiles.tres).
;
; ================= THE FLAG QUESTION, WHICH IS THE WHOLE RISK OF THIS FILE =================
;
; A PassiveDynamicZone is gated on gear.is_dynamic_zone_active (passive_dynamic_zone.gd:13-14), and
; that is a DIFFERENT per-gear flag from the is_aura_active the three PassiveAuras follow
; (gear_core.gd:25 and :28 declare the two side by side). A picture on a flag of its own could
; outlive the mechanic it draws, which is worse than no picture. So the two flags were traced before
; this file was written, and they are set in exactly four places:
;
;   1. spawn        unit_printer.gd:16-21   - BOTH set true, then each pulled down by its own
;                                             passive type's starts_active = false. Paired.
;   2. gear reapply unit_condition.gd:879-880 and :898-899 - the same pairing, line for line.
;   3. owner death  event_service.gd:67-68  - BOTH set false, under one comment that says
;                                             "all auras and zones turn off". Paired.
;   4. the setters  gear_core.gd:293 and :297 - set_dynamic_zone_active and set_aura_active. These
;                                             are the ONLY unpaired writers in the engine, and
;                                             nothing in engine/ calls either: a grep of the whole
;                                             tree finds callers only in content/ (the Drake's
;                                             Fortress Protocol, Hardlight Defense System) and in
;                                             our own action_fungal_network.gd.
;
; So the flags cannot drift on their own; they can only be driven apart by the one script that
; drives them, and that script now sets both in one place (action_fungal_network.gd - read the
; paragraph headed WHY THE PROTOCOL SETS TWO FLAGS). starts_active below is the other half:
; without it this zone would be LIT FROM THE START OF THE SCENE while the auras were still dark,
; which is the exact failure this passive was asked not to have.
;
; ================= WHY THE FX IS A REUSED VANILLA SCENE =================
;
; fxe_nanites.tscn is HORUS' own nanite cloud: a grey particle haze on an icosphere_smoke mesh whose
; root declares lock_height_to = 3, which is LOCK_TO.SURFACE - "sets to surface elevation (terrain
; blocks + setpieces + obstructing units)" (fx_endless.gd:11-18). That is literally the author's
; request: the haze sits ON THE GROUND rather than floating at the token's centre, which is the
; default LOCK_TO.UNIT.
;
; IT IS PICKED OVER THE ALTERNATIVES BECAUSE VANILLA HAS ALREADY ANSWERED THIS EXACT QUESTION.
; mt_hive_drone.tres pairs THAT VERY SCENE with a radius-2 DynamicZone and a range-2 PassiveAura on
; a HORUS deployable - the same radius, the same pairing of picture to aura, the same manufacturer -
; so the game already shows what a burst-2 nanite cloud looks like on this board, and the card here
; is literally "a cloud of nanite spores". fxe_nanobots.tscn and fxe_swarm_body.tscn are the near
; misses (the Hive's razor swarm and HORUS' own Swarm Body). fxe_smoke_cloud.tscn was rejected on
; meaning rather than looks: its only user is mt_shroud_projector_assassin.tres, the one zone in the
; tree that sets BOTH can_see_into and can_see_outof to false, so on this board that haze means "you
; cannot see through this" - which is the one thing this zone deliberately does not do.
;
; NO NEW ART, deliberately: icons and art are SP3's business, and a referenced vanilla .tscn brings
; its own already-imported .ctex with it. The id the engine will look up is the scene's BASENAME
; (`fxe_nanites`, via FxEndless.get_id_from_scene, fx_endless.gd:93-96) resolved through
; ContentLibrary.fxendless_library, which is built by globbing `fxe_*.tscn` under res://content
; (content_library.gd:319-321). A vanilla scene is in that index already; a new one would have to be
; named into it, and a mismatch there is a silent no-draw (content_library.gd:215-219 logs an error
; and returns "", after which FxEndless.create_from_id hands back null and reconstruct_add appends
; nothing, fx_endless.gd:83-91 into fx_endless_controller.gd:72-74).
fxe = ExtResource("3_nanites")
dynamic_zone = SubResource("Resource_shape")
; DARK UNTIL THE PROTOCOL IS PRESSED - the same declaration all three PassiveAuras make, on the
; other flag. passive_dynamic_zone.gd:7-8 spells the semantics out: "If ANY passive dynamic zones on
; this gear set this to false, all dynamic zones on this gear start inactive." Per-GEAR, like the
; aura flag. This Kit has one dynamic zone, so unlike starts_active on the three auras this line is
; NOT redundant with a neighbour - it is the only thing holding the cloud down at spawn, and
; mutating it alone reddens test_the_ground_cloud_is_dark_before_the_protocol (T5-M2).
starts_active = false
; THE MYCONID'S OWN FOUR TILES ARE LEFT CLEAR. passive_dynamic_zone.gd:25 drops any drawn tile the
; unit occupies when this is false, so the cloud is a solid block with a 2x2 hole where the frame
; stands. Both vanilla HORUS nanite zones do the same (mt_hive_drone.tres, ms_swarm_body.tres),
; for the obvious reason that a particle haze over the mech hides the mech - and here it also makes
; the drawn set EXACTLY the set of tiles a hostile can stand in and be caught, since nothing can
; share the Myconid's space without Buff.TO.CAN_SHARE_SPACE or a PassiveAttachment stackup - the
; filter at pathfinder.gd:117-122 and the append at :123-125, which together are the whole of
; can_share_space_units.
;
; It is a one-line flip if the author wants the haze over the frame too; no rule depends on it, and
; test_the_cloud_leaves_the_myconids_own_tiles_clear is what would have to change with it.
is_fxe_at_unit_tiles = false
; is_fxe_at_all_tiles is left at its TRUE default, and it is what makes this a ZONE rather than a
; single puff: false collapses the whole thing to one ticket at the unit's own tile
; (passive_dynamic_zone.gd:28-29), which is the opposite of what was asked for. Mutation T5-M3.
